# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without the working-tree half (eol=lf), Git for Windows' core.autocrlf leaves
# LF files alone on checkout but any tool that rewrites a file with CRLF — pnpm
# touching package.json/lockfiles, a formatter run — makes Git report it as
# modified while the content diff is empty. Pinning eol=lf makes Git normalise
# those writes away instead of surfacing them as phantom changes.
#
# LF is also required, not just tidier: the API images run Linux, and a shell
# script or entrypoint checked out with CRLF fails with `bad interpreter: ^M`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF even if someone overrides the rule above.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by end-of-line conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
